  "prefLabel": "Mec 103.02 Meetings of the Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 103.02 Meetings of the Board.\n\n(a) The board shall elect a chair and a vice chair from among its members.\n\n(b) The chair shall preside over all meetings of the board.\n\n(c) In the absence of the chair at a meeting of the board, the vice chair shall preside.\n\n(d) Notice of all meetings shall be given in such a manner as in accordance with New Hampshire RSA 91-A:2 and RSA 310:5.\n\n(e) Meetings of the board shall be open to the public to the extent required by RSA 91-A and notice of board meetings shall be posted pursuant to RSA 91-A:2 and RSA 310:5.\n\n(f) The annual meeting of the board shall be the first regular meeting held in each state fiscal year.\n\n(g) The office of professional licensure and certification shall provide the board on a quarterly basis an accounting from the agency of moneys derived under the provisions of RSA 153:27 through RSA 153:36.\n\nSource. #10798, eff 3-18-15; ss by #13483, eff 1-9-23 (formerly Saf-Mec 103.02) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 100); #14408, eff 10-17-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec100.html"
